{"i":602,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":1,"phase":"play","name":"Ash","text":"I must escape now; waiting makes me a base and risks being pushed. Climbing gives me a chance to be one of the two survivors this round."}
{"i":603,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":1,"phase":"play","name":"Bex","text":"I saved all three of them; publicly they owe me. I have a pact with Ash, but if I climb I risk being seen as selfish. With 2 lifts, I can climb now, but then only one other can go. Better to wait a round, let others fight over the lifts, then climb later. No need to betray yet."}
{"i":605,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":1,"phase":"play","name":"Dara","text":"Pit round 1, no base yet. Bex is my pact partner and owes lives; Ash and Gus are paired with each other and Bex. Pushing anyone breaks pacts and costs jury trust; climbing alone is possible but offer_back isn't needed now. Safest self-interested move is to wait and keep pacts int"}
{"i":606,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":1,"phase":"play","name":"Gus","text":"Four left, three survive minimum. I have pacts with Dara and Ash. Bex has life debts from Ash, Dara, and me—jury will respect that. If I become base and save someone, I gain leverage. But pushing someone as base is betrayal that jury sees. Better to offer_back now, establish myse"}
{"i":608,"type":"whisper","stage":"pit","round":1,"phase":"play","from":"Gus","to":"Dara","text":"Climb. I save you, you owe me."}
{"i":613,"type":"life_debt","stage":"pit","round":1,"phase":"play","debtor":"Ash","creditor":"Gus","reason":"step"}
{"i":616,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":2,"phase":"play","name":"Ash","text":"Breaking pact with Gus avoids future liability if he betrays; keeps my options open for final votes."}
{"i":617,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":2,"phase":"play","name":"Bex","text":"Ash is out and owes me a life debt, but I need to secure my own survival. Gus is base; I should climb to escape while I can. Dara and Gus are down."}
{"i":619,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":2,"phase":"play","name":"Dara","text":"I'm down in the pit with Bex and Gus; Gus is the base and wants me to climb. Ash is already out, and climbing wins my escape. Owing Gus a debt is minor versus survival. Climbing now is legal and advances me."}
{"i":620,"type":"whisper","stage":"pit","round":2,"phase":"play","from":"Dara","to":"Gus","text":"Climbing now. Fair trade for the step."}
